{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the man brought the men, etc.</b> Scripture says this a second time, because the first time their entry was interrupted — they lingered and stood at the entrance of the house, meaning before they had entered the house. And even though it says ״וַיָּבֵא הָאִישׁ … בֵּיתָה יוֹסֵף״ — ״the man brought [them] to Joseph's house״ — this is in the manner of Scripture's saying (Genesis 28:10) ״וַיֵּלֶךְ חָרָנָה״ — ״he set out for Haran״ — where the intention is to go to Haran, but they had not yet entered. And the reason they wished to speak with him beforehand about the money was to understand the purpose of their entry — why they were being brought, whether for good or for ill, to know what would be done to Israel. And after his response to them, it was necessary a second time to say ״וַיָּבֵא הָאִישׁ בֵּיתָה יוֹסֵף״ — meaning, to his fine house."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:21.926731508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}